on-arrival: recovery_fund_event_done = 1; news_headline = "PiS needs opposition votes for the recovery fund"

= May 2021 — Recovery fund

Poland needs the EU recovery fund, but Solidarna Polska has taken votes away
from Mateusz Morawiecki's majority. Our MPs can now secure safeguards directly,
force KO and Poland 2050 into one control package, or refuse to rescue PiS and
risk leaving the money to somebody else's arithmetic.

- @recovery_deal
- @recovery_opposition
- @recovery_abstain
- @recovery_palace

@recovery_deal
title: Negotiate safeguards with the government and vote yes
subtitle: The historical gamble.
on-arrival: recovery_stance = "Ratification deal"; recovery_fund_strategy = "Negotiated PiS deal"; recovery_fund_ratified = 1; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "Lewica yes votes complete the ratification majority"; pis_relation += 10; ko_relation -= 12; p2050_relation -= 7; relation_pis_psl += 3; rival_relation_pis_psl += 3; labor_credibility += 4; household_policy_pressure += 3; barons_dissent -= 3; progressives_dissent += 5; last_policy_stage = "Negotiated concession"; last_policy_authority = "PiS cabinet and Sejm majority"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Lewica trades its votes for recovery-fund safeguards"

Our votes pass the law and force Morawiecki to acknowledge social and local
safeguards he did not offer freely. PiS calls us responsible; KO calls us its
lifeline. Inside Lewica, the old parliamentary wing celebrates relevance while
progressives ask who will enforce a bargain owned by the cabinet.


- @left_discipline_2021: Turn to the caucus that split on the vote

@recovery_opposition
title: Demand one opposition amendment slate
subtitle: Requires working relations and compatible coalition instincts.
choose-if: ko_relation >= 45 and p2050_relation >= 28 and ko_coalition_openness >= 45 and p2050_coalition_openness >= 42
unavailable-subtitle: At least one opposition partner prefers a separate strategy.
on-arrival: recovery_stance = "Voted against"; recovery_fund_strategy = "Common opposition slate"; recovery_fund_ratified = 1; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "A common opposition yes vote passes ratification with one control package"; ko_relation += 7; p2050_relation += 6; relation_ko_p2050 += 4; rival_relation_ko_p2050 += 4; pis_relation -= 5; constitutional_restraint += 3; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "The opposition writes one recovery-fund control package and ratifies the law"

We arrive with KO and Poland 2050 at one list of controls and vote for the money
without giving Morawiecki a private partner. The opposition proves it can
govern a common interest; PiS tells voters that three rival parties needed a
week to say yes.

- @left_discipline_2021: Turn to the caucus that split on the vote


@recovery_abstain
title: Refuse a bilateral deal and abstain
on-arrival: recovery_stance = "Abstained"; recovery_fund_strategy = "Abstention"; recovery_fund_ratified = 1 if pis_seats + psl_seats >= 231; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "PiS and PSL provide the majority without Lewica" if recovery_fund_ratified = 1; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "No alternative majority reaches 231" if recovery_fund_ratified = 0; pis_relation -= 2; ko_relation -= 3; p2050_relation -= 2; razem_dissent -= 2; public_trust -= 2; government_coalition_dissent += 4; news_headline = "Lewica abstains and leaves ratification to the recorded PiS–PSL count"

[? if recovery_fund_ratified: PSL supplies the votes we withheld. The money
moves forward, PiS learns that another opposition partner is available, and we
own neither the safeguards nor the defeat of the government. ?]

[? if not recovery_fund_ratified: No alternative majority appears. The law
fails without our votes; Razem praises the refusal to rescue PiS while mayors
and unions ask why opposition discipline was worth delaying the fund. ?]

- @left_discipline_2021: Turn to the caucus that split on the vote


@recovery_palace
title: Ask Trzaskowski to sponsor and sign recovery-fund safeguards
subtitle: Cohabitation path: the President may convene, advocate and sign; Parliament and EU institutions still decide ratification and milestones.
view-if: trz_inaugurated = 1
choose-if: president_relation >= 42
unavailable-subtitle: The Palace will not guarantee a package without a working relationship.
on-arrival: recovery_stance = "Palace route"; recovery_fund_strategy = "Presidential sponsorship"; recovery_fund_ratified = 1 if pis_seats + ko_seats + p2050_seats + psl_seats >= 231; recovery_fund_vote_basis = "A Palace-convened cross-party majority ratifies; EU institutions retain milestone control"; president_relation += 7; ko_relation += 5; p2050_relation += 4; psl_relation += 3; pis_relation -= 5; judicial_legitimacy += 4; household_policy_pressure += 3; government_coalition_dissent += 7; trz_right_fragmentation += 10; trz_right_backlash += 5; rival_relation_pis_ko -= 4; last_policy_stage = "Presidential sponsorship"; last_policy_authority = "President may convene and sign; Sejm ratifies"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The President sponsors a recovery-fund control package for a Sejm vote"

We let President Trzaskowski convene the parties and sponsor the safeguards,
while the Sejm supplies the majority and EU institutions retain milestone
control. KO gains the photograph and we gain a package. Solidarna Polska attacks
both Morawiecki and the Palace, widening the governing fracture before the June
rights test.


- @left_discipline_2021: Turn to the caucus that split on the vote

@left_discipline_2021
# prose-audit: Grade B — The suspensions read back the ratification decision and separate a whip question from a merger question; the six suspended deputies are named as a group rather than individually.
title: Six suspensions inside our own caucus
subtitle: The recovery-fund vote becomes a discipline case in the middle of the unification
face-image: img/poland/events/wlodzimierz-czarzasty-2019.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_discipline_2021_done = 1;
Q.party_unity = (Number(Q.party_unity) || 0) - 4;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica's leadership suspends six deputies over the recovery-fund vote";
!}

= May 2021 — Discipline before the merger is finished

The ratification vote is over and our caucus did not go through the lobby as
one body. **Włodzimierz Czarzasty**, who is simultaneously running the
unification of SLD and Wiosna into a single party, suspends six deputies —
**Tomasz Trela** among them — for how they voted and, more precisely, for
saying in public that the leadership had traded the caucus's signature without
asking it.

The timing is the problem. A whip question in an ordinary month is
housekeeping. A whip question during a merger is a demonstration of who will
own the common party's discipline afterwards, and every current in the building
reads it that way, correctly.

[? if recovery_stance = "Ratification deal": We negotiated a deal for the
ratification and the deputies who refused it are being punished for refusing a
bargain they were never shown.?]
[? if recovery_stance = "Voted against": We voted against as a caucus, which
makes six suspensions over the same vote extremely difficult to explain to
anybody.?]
[? if recovery_stance = "Abstained": We abstained, which means the six are being
suspended for having a position at all.?]
[? if recovery_stance = "Palace route": We took the question to the Palace, and
the six were the ones who said out loud that this was not a decision the caucus
had made.?]
[? if merger_resolution != "": The merger settlement in force is **[+
merger_resolution +]**, and it is about to be tested by somebody using it.?]

- @discipline_lift
- @discipline_uphold
- @discipline_arbitration
- @discipline_settlement

@discipline_lift
title: Lift the suspensions and put the whip rule to the caucus
subtitle: Costs the leadership its authority and buys the merger a caucus that believes it has a vote.
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_discipline_result = "Suspensions lifted";
Q.party_unity = (Number(Q.party_unity) || 0) + 6;
Q.labor_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.labor_dissent) || 0) - 6
);
Q.progressives_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.progressives_dissent) || 0) - 5
);
Q.barons_dissent = (Number(Q.barons_dissent) || 0) + 7;
Q.barons_strength = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.barons_strength) || 0) - 2
);
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The suspensions are lifted and the caucus writes its own whip rule";
!}

The six come back and the rule is written by the people it binds: which votes
are whipped, who decides, and what a deputy is entitled to say in public about
a decision they were not part of.

Czarzasty's office has lost an argument in front of every current in the
building, three months before a unification congress. What the common party
gains is a caucus that will not have to be suspended again to be held together.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@discipline_uphold
title: Uphold the suspensions and make the whip the merger's first rule
subtitle: Establishes the leadership's authority over the common party at the price of six deputies who will remember.
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_discipline_result = "Suspensions upheld";
Q.party_unity = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.party_unity) || 0) - 6
);
Q.barons_strength = (Number(Q.barons_strength) || 0) + 3;
Q.barons_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.barons_dissent) || 0) - 5
);
Q.labor_dissent = (Number(Q.labor_dissent) || 0) + 9;
Q.progressives_dissent =
    (Number(Q.progressives_dissent) || 0) + 6;
Q.pps_dissent = (Number(Q.pps_dissent) || 0) + 8;
Q.left_whip_doctrine = "Leadership whip";
Q.news_headline =
    "The leadership upholds the suspensions and sets the common party's whip";
!}

The suspensions stand. The message is received exactly as intended: the party
being built this summer will have one discipline, and it belongs to the people
running the merger.

Six deputies spend the unification congress as spectators with grievances and
telephones. Every splinter conversation that happens in this parliament — and
several happen — starts from the list of people who were suspended in May.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@discipline_arbitration
title: Send it to a binding internal arbitration nobody controls
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Buys procedure instead of a winner; both camps will call it weakness until they need it.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party has no neutral body and no staff to convene one.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources = (Number(Q.resources) || 0) - 1;
Q.left_discipline_result = "Binding arbitration";
Q.left_whip_doctrine = "Arbitrated discipline";
Q.left_arbitration_body = 1;
Q.party_unity = (Number(Q.party_unity) || 0) + 4;
Q.barons_dissent = (Number(Q.barons_dissent) || 0) + 3;
Q.labor_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.labor_dissent) || 0) - 4
);
Q.progressives_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.progressives_dissent) || 0) - 3
);
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "A binding internal arbitration takes the suspensions out of the leader's hands";
!}

Three people none of the currents chose, a written procedure, and a decision
that binds the leadership as much as the deputies. It reinstates four, upholds
two with a reprimand, and satisfies nobody, which is the standard evidence that
an arbitration is real.

The body outlives the case. It is the reason the next internal crisis — and
there is always a next one — is argued in front of somebody rather than
announced by press release.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@discipline_settlement
title: Enforce the merger settlement exactly as written and let it decide
subtitle: Requires an inclusive merger settlement to enforce; it converts a signed document into an actual constitution.
choose-if: merger_resolution = "Five-current truce" or merger_resolution = "Membership ballot" or merger_resolution = "Razem-led current pact" or merger_resolution = "Amnesty and internal appeal"
unavailable-subtitle: There is no protective merger settlement to invoke — the currents never agreed one, so this is a straight test of strength.
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_discipline_result = "Settlement enforced";
Q.left_whip_doctrine = "Settlement discipline";
Q.party_unity = (Number(Q.party_unity) || 0) + 8;
Q.labor_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.labor_dissent) || 0) - 7
);
Q.progressives_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.progressives_dissent) || 0) - 5
);
Q.pps_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.pps_dissent) || 0) - 6
);
Q.barons_dissent = (Number(Q.barons_dissent) || 0) + 4;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The merger settlement is enforced against the leadership that signed it";
!}

The settlement we agreed says what happens to a deputy who dissents on a vote
their current did not authorise, and it says it in terms that bind the chair as
well. We read it out, apply it, and the suspensions are resolved by a document
rather than by whoever is strongest in the room.

That is the moment the settlement stops being a communiqué. Every current now
knows the text can be invoked against the leadership, which is worth
considerably more to the common party than six reinstatements.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue
